    {
      "id": "8bk9rgn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Fire Safety"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fire requires three essential components to exist: Fuel, Heat, and Oxygen, which form the Fire Triangle.",
        "Fires are categorized into distinct classes (Class A, B, C, and D) based on the fuel source.",
        "The PASS method (Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep) is the standard operational procedure for operating portable fire extinguishers.",
        "Workshop fire prevention relies on proper storage of volatile liquids, good housekeeping, and electrical safety.",
        "In a fire emergency, raising the alarm and executing proper evacuation procedures take priority before attempting containment."
      ],
      "id": "oyinwl6"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Fire Triangle Elements",
          "value": "3 Components",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "PASS Method Steps",
          "value": "4 Steps",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Standard Fire Classes",
          "value": "4 Classes (A-D)",
          "icon": "award"
