    {
      "id": "s5nthcg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. PASS Method for Using Fire Extinguishers"
    },
    {
      "id": "5xmxu67",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "P – Pull the safety pin",
        "A – Aim the nozzle at the base of the fire",
        "S – Squeeze the handle",
        "S – Sweep from side to side"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Never use water on electrical or flammable liquid fires; water conducts electricity and spreads liquid fuel.",
        "Class A fires involve wood/paper, Class B involves flammable liquids, Class C involves gases/electrical, and Class D involves burning metals.",
        "Remember the exact sequence of the PASS acronym: Pull the pin, Aim at the base of the fire, Squeeze the lever, Sweep side to side."
      ],
      "id": "c6x45yp"
    },
    {
